WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.200
Just like with the superhero Batman, we've
seen quite a few versions of Catwoman, also

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.529
known as Selina Kyle, over the years.

00:00:07.529 --> 00:00:12.599
From Julie Newmar and Eartha Kitt in the "Batman"
TV series starring Adam West and Burt Ward,

00:00:12.599 --> 00:00:16.790
to Michelle Pfeiffer and Anne Hathaway in
more modern film adaptations, there have been

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:19.350
many changes to the character over time.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:23.110
So when it was announced that Zoë Kravitz
would be taking on the iconic character for

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:27.020
the new "The Batman" movie, fans should've
known to expect something new.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:31.220
In "The Batman," fans get to see a younger
Bruce Wayne, played by Robert Pattinson, in

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:35.000
his early years as the vigilante, and that's
the same case with Selina.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.920
She isn't quite Catwoman yet, though she's
well on her way.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:42.000
While she has all of the skills and the drive
to become the well-known antihero, she's still

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.390
just a young woman with some personal issues
to take care of.

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:48.490
But what else does the 2022 film change about
Selina?

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:52.910
While there are a few stark changes to the
character to note with Kravitz's performance,

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:56.050
there's one glaring difference that drives
the whole movie forward.

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:58.080
Beware: spoilers ahead!

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:03.240
In the original DC "Catwoman" comics, Selina's
parents are Maria and Brian Kyle, who both

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:07.180
tragically die when she is quite young, leading
to her life on the street.

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:10.780
But the version of Selina we see in "The Batman"
doesn't quite have the same experience.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:14.740
Yes, her mother is Maria, but her father is
someone very different.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:18.889
It's noted by many that the comics include
speculation that Selina's real parents aren't

00:01:18.889 --> 00:01:23.030
the Kyles, but are really Carmine Falcone
and his wife, Louisa.

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:27.459
While the comics never explicitly confirm
or deny this, "The Batman" decides to concretely

00:01:27.459 --> 00:01:30.909
change the story and have Falcone be Selina's
father.

00:01:30.909 --> 00:01:35.439
In the movie, Maria works at the Iceberg Lounge
and has a relationship of sorts with the mob

00:01:35.439 --> 00:01:37.590
boss, which results in Selina's birth.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:41.830
There is zero mention of her comic book father
Brian, and it seems unlikely that there ever

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:44.170
would be in possible future films.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:48.420
Selina is completely sure that Falcone is
her father, but after being abandoned by him

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:52.920
after her mother's death (which she later
finds out is his doing), she has no real attachment

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:56.469
to the man, though she holds strong feelings
of resentment and anger.

00:01:56.469 --> 00:02:02.060
So when Bruce uncovers the true depth of Falcone's
crimes, Selina is ever so eager to find Falcone

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:06.159
and take him down, stopping him from doing
anything else while also getting a chance

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:07.780
to confront him about her mother.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:11.700
Add to that the reveal that he's involved
in her roommate's death, and you've got just

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:14.790
about the worst father-daughter relationship
out there.

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:19.040
But aside from the connection with Falcone,
"The Batman" also makes one other small yet

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:21.200
important change to Selina.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:26.099
While this is a very small detail in the new
movie, longtime fans of Catwoman in the DC

00:02:26.099 --> 00:02:30.780
Comics might notice something about the way
Selina interacts with her roommate and coworker

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:31.980
from the Iceberg Lounge.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:36.239
This detail is actually a change from past
screen depictions of Selina, but it makes

00:02:36.239 --> 00:02:39.129
the character more similar to the comic book
version.

00:02:39.129 --> 00:02:43.989
Luckily for those who missed it, Matt Galea
of Pedestrian did not, picking up on hints

00:02:43.989 --> 00:02:48.849
of an intimate relationship between the two
women, especially in how Selina calls her

00:02:48.849 --> 00:02:49.860
"baby."

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:54.900
Selina is frequently depicted as bisexual
in the comics, which is made canon in "Catwoman"

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:55.900
#39.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:03:00.261
So while "The Batman" definitely doesn't confirm
Selina's sexuality, there are hints that this

00:03:00.261 --> 00:03:03.470
aspect of the character may be explored in
further films.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:09.280
Galea was able to ask both Kravitz and director
Matt Reeves about this specific detail directly,

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:13.930
and whether or not it was a purposeful choice
in order to highlight her bisexuality in the

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:14.930
comics.

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:18.459
Kravitz confirmed to Galea for Pedestrian
that although it wasn't written in the script,

00:03:18.459 --> 00:03:23.180
"That's definitely the way I interpreted that,
that they had some kind of romantic relationship."

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:26.280
Reeves wasn't as definitive with his comments,
but he did say that,

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:29.930
"I don't think we meant to go directly in
that way, but you can interpret it that way

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:33.439
for sure ... there was meant to be quite an
intimate relationship between them."

00:03:33.439 --> 00:03:37.140
Based on this, it's certainly worth having
hope that — if Reeves, Kravitz, and others

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:41.519
return for future installments after "The
Batman" — Selina's sexuality will finally

00:03:41.519 --> 00:03:43.709
be accurately presented on screen.

